From: Dominggoes Isakh <drjisakh@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 16:34:19 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] vold: Fix missing <algorithm> include for std::replace

Same issue as bootable/recovery's volume_manager/PublicVolume.cpp:
std::replace() is used but <algorithm> was never included directly,
relying on it being pulled in transitively. The current libc++
prebuilt no longer does that.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Change-Id: I70b95c25fe8f61950b96d01f2b0eab212e1b69c3
---
 model/PublicVolume.cpp | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/model/PublicVolume.cpp b/model/PublicVolume.cpp
index bf7aaa6..04df4ae 100644
--- a/model/PublicVolume.cpp
+++ b/model/PublicVolume.cpp
@@ -33,6 +33,8 @@
 #include <private/android_filesystem_config.h>
 #include <utils/Timers.h>
 
+#include <algorithm>
+
 #include <fcntl.h>
 #include <stdlib.h>
 #include <sys/mount.h>
